        "created_at": "2020-11-24T14:59:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I want to do something different and light-hearted from our very, very melodramatic and somewhat grim stories of the past, well, 2 whole collections.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I have a character I want to use that is like the Impossible Man from Marvel or Mr. Mxyzptlk from DC.&nbsp; I think it's a waste to make an actual villain sheet, as such characters can't be punched to victory.</p>\n<p>I figure the scenario would involve escalating Challenges to Overcome, but I wanted to have some mechanical sense of what this guy can do.&nbsp; Any ideas about how you would do such a scene aside from just arbitrarily adding Challenges as the scene goes on? Or is that the best way to do it? What do you think?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:29.608Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
